o Electronics Corp. side of the GM Hughes unit . Profit at the unit <ei18 fell> to $ 110.6 million , or 37 cents a share , from $ 142.4 million , or 45 cents a share , largely because of a $ 24 million one-time <ei20 charge> associated with Hughes 's previously <ei21 announced> <ei22 plan> to <ei23 reduce> employment by at least 6,000 people by year end . Even excluding the charge , however , net <ei25 fell> 5 % . In addition , GM 's North American vehicle production <ei26 fell> 8.4 % from a year ago , which <ei28 hurt> Delco Electronic 's earnings , a company spokesman <ei29 said> . That <ei30 decline> was reflected in revenue for the GM Hughes unit , which <ei31 edged> down to $ 2.58 billion from $ 2.63 billion . In the nine months , GM Hughes net <ei33 fell> 6.6 % to $ 486.6 million , or $ 1.48 a share , from $ 521 million , or $ 1.58 a share . Revenue <ei34 rose> 3.5 % to $ 8.47 billion from $ 8.18 billion . At GMAC , net <ei35 dropped> 3.1 % to $ 234.5 million from $ 241.9 million . The finance unit <ei36 attributed> the <ei37 decline> to higher borrowing costs compared with a year earlier . GMAC <ei39 said> its automotive financing and leasing business <ei40 rose> 35 % in the U.S., largely because of dealer and customer incentives <ei42 used> to <ei43 boost> sales . GMAC profits are combined with earnings from the rest of GM 's operations and attributed to the company 's traditional common stock . In the first nine months , GMAC 's earnings <ei45 fell> 8 % to $ 859.5 million from $ 930.2 million . At EDS , third-quarter profit <ei47 jumped> 16 % to a record $ 110.9 million , or 93 cents a share , from $ 95.9 million , or 79 cents a share . Revenue <ei48 rose> 12 % to $ 1.37 billion from $ 1.22 billion . In the nine months , EDS <ei50 earned> $ 315.8 million , or $ 2.62 a share , up 13 % from $ 280.7 million , or $ 2.30 a share . Revenue <ei51 rose> 14 % to $ 4.03 billion from $ 3.54 billion . Revenue from non-GM accounts was 45 % of EDS 's total business in th